* 10. FILE PERMISSIONS (rwx) & OWNERSHIP
** Understanding Formats
   - File Types: =-[regular file]=, =d[directory]=, =l[symbolic link]=
   - Triad Blocks: =Owner (u)=, =Group (g)=, =Others (o)=, =All (a)=
   - Value Keys: =r = 4 (read)=, =w = 2 (write)=, =x = 1 (execute)=, =- = 0 (no permission)=
** Numeric Mapping Examples
   - 755 :: =rwxr-xr-x= (Full owner control, read/execute access for others)
   - 644 :: =rw-r----= (Read/Write owner privileges, read-only balance)
   - 700 :: =rwx------= (Full owner control isolated from everyone else)
** Change Permissions (chmod)
   - chmod u+x <file>   :: Add execute permission parameter to owner
   - chmod g+w <file>   :: Add write permission tracking to group
   - chmod o-r <file>   :: Remove read permissions from others
   - chmod a+r <file>   :: Add read permissions to everyone globally
   - chmod go=r <file>  :: Hard-set group and others to read-only access
   - chmod 755 <file>   :: Explicitly apply 755 permissions
   - chmod -R 755 <dir> :: Recursively change nested directory permissions layout
** Change Ownership (chown / chgrp)
   - chown <user> <file>          :: Reassign owner of a file
   - chown <user>:<group> <file>  :: Reassign both user owner and group owner targets simultaneously
   - chown -R <user>:<group> <dir>:: Recursively cascade ownership over target directory trees
   - chgrp <group> <file>         :: Reassign file group parameter
   - chown --reference=<file1> <file2> :: Duplicate permission mappings from file1 onto file2
** Special Bits Configuration
   - SetUID (4)     :: Executed with target file owner level privilege access. Syntax: =chmod u+s <file>=
   - SetGID (2)     :: Executed with directory/group assigned rights. Syntax: =chmod g+s <dir>=
   - Sticky Bit (1) :: Only file owners can erase files in target folder. Syntax: =chmod +t <dir>=
** Umask Configs
   - Default security masks for establishing fresh filesystem entries.
   - Files Calculation: =666 - umask = permissions=
   - Directories Calc: =777 - umask = permissions=
   - 022 (Standard mask) -> Files: 644, Dirs: 755
   - 077 (High restriction) -> Files: 600, Dirs: 700

